# Atlas service environment — TEMPLATE.
#
# The real file is host state, never part of a release:
#   ~/atlas-data/env/atlas.env     mode 600, owner ocelia
# A deploy verifies it exists and never writes it (JAM standards/secrets.md).

# --- RestaurantOS peer API (atlas-restaurantos-api.service) -----------------
# Required. Bearer token JARVIS presents; at least 24 characters. Generate with
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# The same value goes in JARVIS's env file as ATLAS_API_TOKEN.
ATLAS_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. Bearer token for the Atlas briefings phone app; at least 24
# characters, different from ATLAS_API_TOKEN. Accepted ONLY on the briefing
# routes (GET /v1/health, /v1/briefings, /v1/briefings/{id}); it opens nothing
# else. Leave empty to let only ATLAS_API_TOKEN read briefings. Generate it the
# same way as ATLAS_API_TOKEN and paste it into the app, never into JARVIS.
ATLAS_BRIEFINGS_TOKEN=

# Optional. Loopback port the API listens on. Default 8790.
# ATLAS_API_PORT=8790
